WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.940
Takaido-fushinari cucumbers, growing healthily.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.720
Wase-shinkuro eggplants,
almost ready for harvest.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.270
Probably within a few days.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.700
Aside from the ruptured tomatoes, everything's on track for this year.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.500
Hello?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.160
This is Tamo Agricultural and
Forestry High School, Aota Hall.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:26.480
Hello?

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.080
Kei-kun.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.600
<i>You</i>.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.800
How did you find me?

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.740
Did you think you could escape me?

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.050
Now be good and come back.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.260
I refuse!

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.850
I've cut all ties with you!

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.960
I will be paying you a visit soon.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.340
Make sure you're ready.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.360
<i>It began with a single phone call.</i>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.030
<i>The demons from my past
were catching up with me.</i>

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.160
Oh no!

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.170
This is terrible!

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.630
What is it? You seem panicked.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.300
Well, you see,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.010
the principal's snapped!

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.020
Huh? Snap...?

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:42.970
What?!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.490
<i>Th-That's</i> the principal?

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:54.310
The guy who, according to legend, killed a bear unarmed?

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.190
Oh?

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.660
Who might you laddies and lassies be?

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:04.820
Sensei, why did you bring us to see the principal?

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.360
It has to do with eggplants!

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.440
Eggplants?

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.370
Eggplant... Eggplant...

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.250
Our poor principal keeps begging for eggplants.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.100
We got heaps of eggplants 'round here.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.880
Hain't you tried feedin' him some?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:24.260
Well, Becky tried, but he kept
insisting, "This isn't eggplant!"

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.470
Becky was like, totes flaming mad!

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.220
What kind of eggplants did you feed him?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.600
These.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.560
Nothing appears to be amiss about them.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.940
But it didn't work.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.580
So Becky decided her only choice was
to stuff him with our school-grown eggplants.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.060
That's why she called you.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.460
To put it simply,

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:46.760
you are hoping the sincere efforts of
his students will bring him to his senses

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.220
in a heartwarming turn of events.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.100
How cliché.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.120
Dang, this gal don't pull her punches!

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.700
The principal is correct.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.700
Those are not real eggplants.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.580
They're manufactured goods.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.180
M-Manufactured goods?

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.050
What gave you that idea, Kamatori Kei?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.740
Becky tasted them herself!

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.340
She took their firm, fresh, glistening shafts

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.230
and caressed them with her lips.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.730
I would like to request

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.660
the use of the home economics room
at noon tomorrow.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.690
I'll show you what a real eggplant is.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.070
Eggplant...

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.540
So, let's see these "real eggplants" of yours.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.040
If they're icky, nasty eggplants,

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.670
then maybe Becky will take <i>your</i> icky, nasty eggplant as a reward.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:39.930
As you wish.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.760
H-Hold on, Kamatori Kei!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.050
That's not the kind of bet you casually accept!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.890
All right, Becky will start with the eggplants she prepared.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.600
All-organic, pesticide-free,
top-quality eggplants!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.100
500 yen apiece!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:53.980
Five—

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:54.820
Is that a lot?

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.140
Are you off yer rocker?

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.270
You bet it's a lot!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.270
Okay, now it's your turn, Kamatori-kun.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.610
I've brought this.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.840
Wait, Kamatori-kun, are you <i>serious</i>?

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.670
I could pick up something
nicer at the supermarket!

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:19.200
I ask only that you have a taste.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.170
I'll hear your complaints after that.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.660
Oh? Hoh? Hm?

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.010
Well, have it your way.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:28.820
Gulp.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:29.930
Looks good.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.120
Yeah.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:34.230
But the moisture's been cooked out of Becky-sensei's,

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.800
while Kei's looks the same as before.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.580
Not to mention, his seeds are bigger.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.270
Looks like the inside was
as crappy as the outside!

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.230
It's the taste that counts.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.690
Let's start with Becky-sensei's.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.560
It's as good as you'd expect.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.620
That price tag warn't for nothin'!

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.500
It tastes a bit grassy.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.410
Plus, the skin is tough.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.580
That's just the distinctive taste that eggplants have!

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.840
Next up is Kei's eggplant.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:05.960
Eggplant...

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.760
Th-The principal!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:14.930
Sir?!

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:38.680
That's... what... I'm... <i>talking about</i>!

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:43.420
A fruit positively bursting
with satisfying richness!

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:47.920
Fleshy and moist, yet not watery.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.740
With a single bite, the flavor fills your mouth!

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.260
This creamy, smooth texture!

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.650
Forsooth, this is the taste of rejuvenation!

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:01.640
Sir?

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.000
Are you okay?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.800
Thank you for the food.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.860
'Twas most excellent.

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:09.860
Kamatori-kun,

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.320
this, now <i>this</i>, is a <i>real</i> eggplant.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.340
But wherever did you find such a thing?

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.790
I've been growing these
eggplants on my own time.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:23.250
Still, why is the taste so drastically different?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.210
I'm using different seeds.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.220
Of course!

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.160
The quality of the field doesn't matter if the seed—

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.860
My eggplants are heirloom plants.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.840
These are traditional cultivars.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.300
They look unattractive,
and they're a lot of work,

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.430
but they preserve the flavors of the past.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:41.320
On the other hand, the eggplants you've been eating

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.560
have all been F1.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.310
F... 1?

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.480
First filial generation.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.280
A first-generation hybrid
of two purebred cultivars.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:54.100
These hybrids prioritize shape,
productiveness, and efficiency over taste,

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:55.820
and are only grown for one generation.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:57.420
Efficiency?

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.860
Because efficiency is a priority,

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.840
F1 cultivars are grown in highly artificial environments,

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:14.510
with generous amounts of
chemical fertilizer and pesticide.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.890
If those aren't "manufactured goods",
then what are they?

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:22.100
Kamatori-kun, you make a solid argument.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.600
I'm merely stating the truth.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.820
Then how about this?

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:30.190
There is a summer study abroad program
that explores agriculture around the world.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:33.620
Yoshida Kochou-kun and Kamatori Kei-kun,

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:35.500
would you be interested?

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:40.580
I-I <i>have</i> heard that large-scale
agriculture is booming in the West.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.430
There's certainly much I could learn there.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:48.200
B-But going overseas alone with Kamatori Kei...

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.560
Peopow migh' hink we'w on a honeywoon ow fumfing...

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:54.020
I have no interest in foreign agriculture.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:09:01.770
I came here to study about small-scale, local, organic agriculture.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.100
Excuse me.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.020
Y-You!

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.220
How convenient.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.230
You're already here, Kei.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:14.940
I'm saved the trouble of summoning you.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.860
I hope you've prepared yourself.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:18.380
Kei?

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:19.250
Prepared?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.420
I done know this feller!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:24.920
He was on "Gaia's Sunrise" that one time!

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.460
Menjou, president and CEO of Hexa Techs!

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:29.670
Hecks a...?

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.000
A whoppin' big corporation that grows, ships, and sells produce.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.930
And he's the top man!

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.640
Which means Kamatori Kei...

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.310
He is my son.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.240
No!

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.770
You're <i>nothing</i> to me,
much less my father!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.080
Are you his homeroom teacher?

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.150
Yes, and single!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.920
Fill out the paperwork for my son's transfer to another school.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.150
Yes, and single!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.420
Pack your belongings at once.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:02.160
I cannot allow you to fool about in such a place any longer.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:02.870
You have no right—

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.870
What do you mean, "such a place"?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.420
R-Ringo?

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:08.520
Answer me.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.960
What's wrong with this place?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:18.500
This school grows the tastiest vegetables in Japan—no, the world!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.720
It's the best school you'll ever find!

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.920
The tastiest vegetables in the world?

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:28.060
Wh-What's so funny?!

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:32.520
Such ludicrous ideas from
a mere agricultural student.

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:36.380
For someone who grows nothing but artificial, manufactured F1 hybrids,

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:37.530
that's awfully hypocritical!

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.950
Are you claiming that <i>you</i>
can grow good vegetables?

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.200
Better than yours, at least.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:47.800
Very well, Kei.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.370
Let's put that to the test.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:50.830
Test?

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:55.960
A competition to see whether
your vegetables or mine sell better.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:00.040
If I win, you'll quit the agricultural industry forever!

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.850
Those are my conditions!

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.040
I accept.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.600
And if I win,

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.700
you will leave this school!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.580
It's settled.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:22.300
This is where I've been raising
heirloom plants on my own time.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.950
So this is where you up and
disappear off to sometimes.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.870
You maintain all these different vegetables yourself?

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.240
That's right.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.750
My goal is to popularize
traditional cultivars again.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.750
Unlike him, my main priority is not profit,

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.760
but truly delicious vegetables.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:44.640
Kei, is your real name Menjou, not Kamatori?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.040
Kamatori is my aunt's name.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.920
I asked her to adopt me.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:49.840
Adopt?

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:51.230
What drove you to do that?

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.690
<i>His</i> utter depravity!

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:58.420
He may be a skilled businessman,

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:01.690
but he lacks every virtue
someone in agriculture ought have!

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:06.400
So when you said you warn't
interested in studyin' abroad...

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.990
Even if it's on a small scale,

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.870
I want to grow crops that
bring out the best of the region.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.920
The last thing I want to do is end up like <i>him</i>.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:19.120
I grew up on a melon farm.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:25.550
Without pesticides, melons are easily susceptible to pests.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:30.260
My mother's body couldn't handle exposure to pesticides.

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:34.270
But he continued to use them in the name of efficiency, until...

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:35.730
You can't mean...

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:39.120
So callous and greedy is he,

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:43.480
that he continues to use the
pesticides that killed his wife.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.280
He's beyond redemption to me!

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.820
I see.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:51.400
So you think pesticide need not
and should not be used.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:56.230
I regret getting you all involved in our contest.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.920
But please, lend me your help!

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.400
Of course!

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.520
Right, Yoshida-san?

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:02.850
R-Right.

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:07.990
Whether Kamatori Kei transfers schools is of no consequence to me,

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:10.180
but I have Tamo Agricultural's pride to defend!

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:11.580
Darn tootin'!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:14.180
He ain't gonna act all hoity-toity 'bout <i>our</i> school!

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:15.440
Ain't that right, Ringo-cchi?

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:16.710
Absolutely.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.400
We'll have him begging for mercy.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:21.110
You have my thanks.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.520
We will compete to see who sells the most in one hour.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.780
I assume we're competing in proceeds, not profit.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.160
That's right.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.240
But we're working with the same amount of space.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.750
Low price, high volume tactics
aren't going to work.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.120
I don't need you to tell me that.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.210
You should worry more about yourself.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.800
Kei, we need to decide on our pricing soon.

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:47.510
Make them the same as his.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.840
My vegetables are all-organic and pesticide-free.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.220
Taste will be the key to victory!

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.100
Looks like a slick operation you got going here.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.560
Y-You're Money Kanegami!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:58.600
Allow me to help.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:04.680
With Class D's sales tactics,
any produce you got will sell out, guaranteed.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.490
We'll leave the competition in the dust!

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.150
What's the spray bottle for?

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.700
Just watch.

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:11.410
Whoa!

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:15.410
They look freshly picked and still covered in morning dew!

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:17.790
Your attention please.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:22.040
We will be having a limited-time sale on fresh produce in the parking lot.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:22.880
All right!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.510
Let's sell, sell, and sell till we drop!

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:29.220
It looks fresh, but it's oddly shaped.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.260
There are bug bites too.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.510
That's the mark of organic, pesticide-free vegetables!

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.100
The taste will blow you away!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.100
That's true.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.020
The bugs clearly think it tastes good too.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:38.890
I'll take it!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.480
Thank you!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:41.650
Excellent.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.610
No movement on the Hexa Techs side yet.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.980
We're only getting warmed up.

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:48.610
Let's keep 'em on their toes!

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.820
Wh-What are you doing?

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.200
Just sit back and watch.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.870
Th-This is...

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:58.330
Merchandising, my friend.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:14:59.830
Mer-chan? Who's that?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.830
Listen, chief. It's summer.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:02.340
Listen, chief. It's summer.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.590
Plus, it's Friday, the start of the weekend.

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.710
Which means...

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:06.840
Which means?

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.220
Plenty of families will want
to splurge a bit on a rich meal.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.430
At the same time, they'd prefer something easy.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.300
In that case...?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.560
Korean barbecue's on the menu.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.010
Barbecue!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.890
Korean barbecue <i>does</i> sound good!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.310
A great way to get your veggies!

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:25.020
Merchandising, in essence,

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:29.990
is providing the appropriate products,
with the appropriate quantity and price,

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.660
at the appropriate time.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.530
M-My God!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.990
She's a genius who's descended upon the supermarket!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.210
The only promotion they're
doing is free samples.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.370
We've got this. We can do it!

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:45.790
Our side is attracting way more customers!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.630
Our bag of tricks isn't empty yet.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.340
You mean there's more?

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.970
Marketing, baby.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.470
We're talking sales promotion.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.140
Specifically, promotional models!

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.800
B-Booth babes?!

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:00.930
Always thankful, calm, kind, and just!

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.190
NOL48!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:12.110
C'mon gal, ain't no use bein' bashful!

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:13.240
Let's get moving.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.200
Got enough veggies in your life?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:23.830
By leveraging their voice, youth, and cuteness, we'll both draw customers' attention

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.830
and boost their desire to spend.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:27.920
There's more!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.960
To secure the valuable male
demographic at a supermarket,

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.560
we'll throw in "stick it in" vouchers!

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.050
"Stick it in"... vouchers?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:37.800
You get to pick a girl and a vegetable, and she'll stick it in for you.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.890
S-So you're going <i>that</i> route!

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:45.770
We can't play by the book when we're against Hexa Techs' brand power.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.400
G-Good point.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.190
So does that mean, well...

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.480
<i>L-Like this?</i>

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.410
Our dreams come true!

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.620
You're not in this alone!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.580
Woodman Rintarou!

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:05.330
And also...

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:09.000
We're here to give that crusty old dom a taste of being a sub.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.800
Now, let us settle this duel!

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.800
No way! The Four Farm Deities are all here!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.430
Your teacher's here to help out too!

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:23.430
She'll do anything for
one of her own students!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:27.240
Kamatori-kun, you can call Becky "Mommy".

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.940
Go on, say "Mommy".

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:30.860
Don't be shy!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:31.900
Hurry up and say it!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.610
<i>Say it</i>, you little bitch!

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.740
<i>Say my fucking name</i>!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.360
Chief!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:36.860
Roger!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.910
Quit squirming!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:45.120
Open up! Open up!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.160
Welcome!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.540
How's that eggplant look,
sittin' pretty in them boobs?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.790
Ain't it nice and plump? Ain't it?

00:17:52.790 --> 00:17:54.550
I could die of embarrassment!

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.590
Exhibitionism is hardly niche.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.470
You can do it, Boobs-san.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.090
"B-Boobs-san"?

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.560
Dinner is served!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.060
C'mon, baby, have a taste of my eggplant.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.060
My cucumber hangs to the right.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.520
Hey, yo! That's a fine tomato!

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.820
Becky wanna... harvest your... vegetables too!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:36.460
E-Even after all that,

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:39.800
we still couldn't topple the Hexa Techs brand?

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.430
What caused our defeat?

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.680
Was it the brand recognition—

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:43.890
Not at all.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:44.890
What?!

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:48.890
Have a taste.

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.100
The rest of you too.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:57.610
This is—

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.940
It's good.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.820
As good as you'd expect.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:02.780
I-Impossible!

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.240
That can't be!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:16.340
You rejected Hexa Techs' produce on principle

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.260
and challenged me without once tasting it.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.590
So close-minded you were.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.550
That was your undoing!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:29.480
How much time do you devote each day to your vegetables?

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.770
One hour? Two hours?

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.810
At most, perhaps five or six?

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:39.030
We at Hexa Techs deal with vegetables twenty-four hours a day!

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:43.070
Produce grown by a child in his spare time
couldn't possibly compare!

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.570
Don't sugarcoat what you're doing!

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.840
All you do is oversee the growth of F1 hybrids!

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:50.540
And what is wrong with making use of superior technology?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.540
Do you claim that crops grown by only natural means

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:59.000
are more sacred than those that have been studied and improved?

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:01.630
You're undermining the entire history of agriculture!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:05.390
A-All I'm... trying to say...

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.010
is that what you're doing...

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:11.060
is despicable and greed-driven...

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:15.480
I grow vegetables that are
safer, cheaper, and tastier!

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:19.270
What is despicable about that, I ask?

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.690
You fool!

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:23.150
You...

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:29.700
You're insulting not only the agricultural industry
but also the consumers!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.460
I-I've...

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.960
always put the consumer first...

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.210
That's why...

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.170
That's why I wanted to grow organic, pesticide-free...

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.380
Don't you get it already?

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:49.470
You're merely forcing your own
naïve ideals upon the consumers.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:53.180
Can you grow tasty vegetables without chemical fertilizer and pesticide?

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:58.270
True quality produce requires advanced farming techniques and experience.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.440
Do you have either?

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:04.030
Well, we do.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.820
Hexa Techs did not triumph due to brand power.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.280
I admit defeat.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:14.250
Take me wherever you want!

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:23.550
No. I changed my mind.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:24.260
What?!

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:28.300
My company has not stooped low enough that I would make my successor

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.720
a boy who grows such shoddy produce.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.390
What you do is no longer my concern.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:33.640
What?!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:38.810
If you're not satisfied, then grow vegetables that are better than mine!

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.370
So you changed your mind
about studying abroad.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.920
I have to know my enemy to defeat him.

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:02.250
I'll start by seeing what's
out there in the world.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:06.010
But golly, our gal's mighty tardy.

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.340
I wonder what happened.

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:09.760
Sorry I'm late!

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:16.730
You look like a bride fixin' to go on her honeymoon.

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.610
Wh-Wh-What wash tat?!

00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:20.400
D-D-Don't you get the wong idea!

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:22.310
This is abwout mannyers! E-Etiquette!

00:22:22.310 --> 00:22:25.530
You hicksh know noffing about oversheas trabel!

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:28.490
C-Come on, Kamatori Kei.

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:29.150
Sure.

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:31.120
Well, I'll be seeing you.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:32.870
Yep. Have a safe trip!

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:34.620
Buy us lotsa souvenirs!

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:35.830
Have fun.

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:39.390
"A Bright Farming Village".
